  "raw_text": "42\n\nBawaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nBauaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto submit, to bow, to squat, to humble oneself, to prostrate oneself, to bow down, to duck, to\ndodge\n \n/ someterse, inclinarse, ponerse en cuclillas, humillarse, postrarse, resignarse, agacharse, esquivar\n \n(See also/\nVer también:\n \nLula krikaia\n)\n\n(Note/Nota: From the English word:\n \nbow\n \n/ De la palabra inglesa:\n \nbow\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu-09/19\n):\n \nYawan ridi sa ki Jehova ra bawaia dukiara?\n \n–\n \nAre we ready to submit to Jehovah?\n \n/ ¿Estamos listos para\nsometernos a Jehová?)\n\nBawan lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nBawaia\n \nlâka)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhumility, mildness, submission\n \n/ humildad, apacibilidad\n, sumisión\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n:\n \ndb\n \nuses this at\n \nGal\nesha\n \n5:23\n \nto translate\n \nmildness\n, but\n \nfy18\n \nuses\n \nLaman lâka\n \nwhen\n \nquoting\n \nGal\nesha\n \n5:23\n \n/\n \ndb\n\nusa esta en\n \nGal\nesha\n \n5:23\n \npara traducir\n \napacibilidad\n, pero\n \nfy\n \nusa\n \nLaman lâka\n \ncuando cita\n \nGal\nesha\n \n5:23\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n09/19\n):\n \nDîa dukia nani sip sa wan bawanka lâka ba traika kaikaia?\n \n–\n \nWhat things can test our humi\nl\nity?\n \n/\n \n¿Qué\n\ncosas pueden poner a prueba nuestra hum\nil\ndad?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n08/20\n):\n \nBawan lâka bara tânkira ni Gâd lamara tauki kap\n \n–\n \nBe walking close to God with humility and modesty\n\n/ Andemos junto a Dios\n \ncon humildad y modestia\n)\n\nBawan lâka tikpara\n \n(v\n-\nimp)\n \n–\n \ndon’t lose humility, remain humble\n \n/ no pierda la humildad,\n \npermanezca\n\nhumilde\n\nBawikira\n \n(a/t:\n \nBauikira\n)\n \n–\n \n(adj,adv)\n \n–\n \nhumble, lowly, humbly, modest, meek\n \n/ humilde, modesto, manso (\nmwb-\n12/18\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nD\nî\na muni yawan bawikira kaia sa\n \nki?\n \n–\n \nWhy must we be humble?\n \n/\n \n¿Por qué debemos ser humildes?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n07/20\n):\n \nUpla nani\n \nwan mayunbia taim yawan bawikira kaia sa\n \n–\n \nWhen people praise us, we must be humble\n \n/\n\nCuando la gente nos alab\ne\n, debemos ser humildes\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n03/22\n):\n \nBan bawikira kaia dukiara, d\nî\na ba hilp wan munbia?\n \n–\n \nWhat will help us in order to remain humble?\n \n/\n\nQué puede ayudarnos a seguir siendo humildes?\n)\n\nBaw\ni\nkira lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhumble way\n \n/\n \nmanera humilde, con humildad\n\nUpla bawikira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhumble person\n \n/\n \npersona humilde\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n09/19\n):\n \nJehova mita ai uplika bawikira nani ra yamni kaikisa\n \n–\n \nJehovah loves humble people\n \n/\n \nJehová\n\nama a las personas humildes\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n09/19\n):\n \nDîa muni\n \nupla wala nani ba piu bani\n \nbawikira uplika kum lamara kaia want sa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhy do\n\nother people always want to be close to a humble person\n \n/\n \n¿Por qué otras personas siempre quieren estar cerca\n\nde una persona humilde?\n)\n\nBetel watla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nBethel\n \n/ Betel\n\nBetel apiska\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nBethel Office, Branch Office\n \n/ Oficina de Betel, Sucursal\n\nBetel ra Wark Taki nani dukiara Skulka\n \n–\n \nBethel Entrants’ School\n \n/ Escuela\n \nde Nuevos Betelitas\n\nBetel uplika nani Pura Kaiki Daknika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nPersonnel Committee\n \n/\n \nComité de personal\n\nBiara\n \n(\nfy,km\n,bm,db,dbta\n;\n \nByar\n-\nlv,bh,my,sln,lrw,dba,bw\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe interior part of anything, belly, bowels, stomach,\n\nintestine, abdomen, womb\n \n/\n \nla parte interior de cualquier cosa, barriga,\n \npanza,\n \nintestinos, estómago, abdomen, matriz\n\n(Construct:\n \nBiayra\n \n–\n \nmy stomach\n \n/ mi estomago;\n \nBiamra\n \n–\n \nyour stomach\n \n/ tu estomago;\n \nAi biara\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their stomach\n \n/ su\nestomago)\n\nBiara bangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fill the stomach\n \n/ llenar el estomago\n\nBiara bangki takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto come to fill the stomach\n \n/ venir a llenar el estomago\n\nBiara klauhisa\n \n–\n \n(his/her) stomach aches\n \n/ su estómago le duele\n\nBiara m\nâ\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfruit of the womb, any lump in the stomach\n \n/ fruto del vientre, cualquier bulto en el estómago\n\nBiara para\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nBiarapara\n,\n \nBiara parra\n,\n \nBiarpara\n)\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nsterile, barren\n \n/\n \nestéril\n\nBiara plapaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have diarrhea\n \n/\n \ntener diarrea\n\nBiara plapan\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nd\niarrhea\n \n/\n \ndiarrea\n\nBiara sirpika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsmall intestine\n \n/ intestino delgado\n\nBiara tarka\n \n(a/t:\n \nBiara tarkika\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nlarge intestine\n \n/\n \nintestino grueso\n\nBiara yahpirra\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nbig\n-\nbellied\n \n/\n \npanza grande\n\nBiawaia\n \n(v-intrans)\n \n–\n \nto become thin, to become meager, to lose weight\n \n/ enflaquecerse, adelgazarse, perder peso\n\nBiawan\n \n(v-3p-past/pasado, adj)\n \n–\n \nthin, meager, skinny\n \n/ delgado, magro, flaco\n\nBibi\n \n(a/t:\n \nBebi\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbaby\n \n/ bebé\n\n(Construct:\n \nBibiki\n;\n \nBibikam\n;\n \nBibika\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-21\n):\n \nBibikam wal pulisma taim, G\nȃ\nd dîa dukia nani paskan ba dukiara aisas.\n \n–\n \nWhen you play with your baby, talk about\nthe things God has made.\n \n/ Cuando juegue con su bebé, hable de las cosas que Dios ha hecho.)",
